\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Privacy Policy for Portion Clarity\
\
Effective date: November 7, 2026\
\
Portion Clarity is wibe-developed by Milko.\
\
## Data Collection\
\
Portion Clarity does not collect, transmit, sell, or share personal data.\
\
The app does not require an account and does not use advertising, analytics, tracking technologies, remote food databases, or third-party data services.\
\
## Nutrition Labels and Photos\
\
Nutrition-label recognition is performed on the device using Apple frameworks. Images selected from the photo library or captured with the camera are processed locally and are not uploaded to the developer or any external service.\
\
## Locally Stored Information\
\
Saved foods, point history, formula settings, and preferences are stored locally on the user\'92s device.\
\
This information is removed when the user deletes the app, unless it is retained by an operating-system backup managed by the user.\
\
## Camera and Photo Library\
\
Camera access is used only when the user chooses to scan a nutrition label. Photo-library access is used only when the user chooses an existing label image.\
\
## Notifications\
\
If the user grants notification permission, Portion Clarity may send an on-device notification when the configured daily point limit is reached. Notification information is not sent to the developer.\
\
## Children\'92s Privacy\
\
Portion Clarity does not knowingly collect personal information from children or other users.\
\
## Changes to This Policy\
\
This policy may be updated if the app\'92s privacy practices change. The effective date above will identify the latest revision.\
\
## Contact\
\
For privacy questions, contact the developer through the support information provided on the Portion Clarity App Store listing.}